1
00:00:01,160 --> 00:00:03,320
Hi everyone. In this tutorial, I'm going

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:05,000
to show you how to add and manage your

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,360
tasks and lists in Blitzit,

4
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:09,200
which is the core of staying organized

5
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,080
and productive.

6
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:13,400
Let's start with lists. Lists help you

7
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,920
organize your tasks by project, area of

8
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:18,360
work, or any category you like.

9
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:19,920
Think of them as folders that keep your

10
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:22,000
tasks grouped.

11
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,720
To create a new list, click the create

12
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:26,400
new list button in the home section.

13
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,120
Give your list a name,

14
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:30,280
pick an icon, adjust the color,

15
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,599
and hit create.

16
00:00:32,599 --> 00:00:34,440
You can always edit your lists later by

17
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:36,280
clicking the three-dot menu next to the

18
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,800
list name.

19
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:40,400
Let's open the list.

20
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,560
Inside each list, tasks are organized

21
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:43,880
into columns.

22
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:45,880
They help you prioritize and schedule

23
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:47,320
your work.

24
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:49,040
You'll see columns titled today, that

25
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:51,000
shows tasks planned for the current day,

26
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,880
this week, that includes tasks for the

27
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:54,920
rest of the week, while the progress bar

28
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:57,120
reflects progress on both today and this

29
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:59,840
week tasks, and backlog. This one is for

30
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:02,360
the tasks scheduled beyond one week.

31
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:04,199
So, this way you know what needs your

32
00:01:04,199 --> 00:01:07,280
immediate attention and what can wait.

33
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:08,880
Blitzit lets you switch between single

34
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:11,040
list view, where you focus on one

35
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:13,560
project at a time, and all lists view,

36
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:15,640
which shows all your tasks across every

37
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:17,280
list in one place.

38
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,000
This flexibility helps you zoom in to

39
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,240
stay focused on one project or get the

40
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:23,080
full picture of all of your tasks

41
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,080
whenever you need it.

42
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:27,400
Adding tasks is simple. Just click the

43
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:30,480
add task button, type your task, and

44
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:33,360
press enter or the confirm button.

45
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:35,400
You can add as many tasks as you want,

46
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,880
and move them by dragging to change the

47
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:38,320
priority.

48
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:41,600
The top tasks are your highest priority.

49
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:43,520
When you hover over a task, you can see

50
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,560
more options available. You can add

51
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:48,320
subtasks, add notes,

52
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:50,200
and move the task between columns with

53
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:52,400
arrow buttons.

54
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:53,960
The same thing can be done by simply

55
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:56,160
dragging and dropping the task.

56
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:58,040
The three-dot menu lets you schedule the

57
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:00,840
task, move it to another list, duplicate

58
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:02,840
it, or delete it.

59
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:05,640
Here you can also see an EST button.

60
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:07,400
By pressing it, you can add a task time

61
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,440
estimate. That is the time you give

62
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:11,480
yourself to complete the task.

63
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:13,080
Enter the amount of hours and minutes

64
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:15,560
and hit enter.

65
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,360
You can also add task time estimates

66
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:19,040
when you create a task by entering the

67
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:21,400
time in the EST field.

68
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,040
Note that if your task is in a live

69
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:25,320
timer, you can only add the EST while

70
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:28,200
pausing the timer.

71
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:30,160
When your task goes into a live timer,

72
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:32,360
Blitzit starts tracking time taken, the

73
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:33,959
actual time you've spent working on the

74
00:02:33,959 --> 00:02:35,959
task so far.

75
00:02:35,959 --> 00:02:37,880
You can also input it manually using

76
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:41,360
this field in the same format as EST.

77
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:43,040
Comparing your estimates with real time

78
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:45,680
helps you improve your planning.

79
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,320
When you complete a task, mark it as

80
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:49,640
done by clicking the checkbox next to

81
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:50,959
it.

82
00:02:50,959 --> 00:02:53,080
You can do it from the list section. The

83
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:54,760
task will move to the done section,

84
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:56,680
giving you that satisfying sense of

85
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,120
progress.

86
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,440
Or you can do it in Blitz mode by

87
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,880
pressing done button in the task field.

88
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:03,080
Congrats.

89
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:04,200
Here you can see that you finished the

90
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:07,440
task 525 minutes early.

91
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:08,880
Not bad.

92
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:10,760
This way you see how many minutes early

93
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,480
or late you finished compared to your

94
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:13,959
EST.

95
00:03:13,959 --> 00:03:15,680
Now you can move to the next task, or

96
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:18,800
maybe it's time to finally take a break.

97
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:22,080
Yeah, that's a good idea.

98
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,840
Check out our other tutorials on the

99
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,320
help center for more tips on using

100
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:27,000
different features on Blitzit to

101
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,440
supercharge your productivity.

102
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,880
And be sure to join our Discord

103
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:32,959
community. There is a lot going on that

104
00:03:32,959 --> 00:03:35,160
will help you optimize your workday.

105
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:37,640
See you.